{"ts":"2026-08-30T12:35:27.802Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"f237494c9fe27db071e2f599","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.251","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-30T12:35:27.802Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Second instance of this item's own failure mode, observed while landing the change that filed it.\n\npnpm quality:static passed locally at exit 0 and Gates (static) failed hosted, this time on ESLint. The cause is a different divergence from the ambient-state one this item describes: the local script pnpm quality:static does not include pnpm lint:eslint, while the hosted Gates (static) job runs both. So the command the contributing guide points at as the local equivalent of a hosted gate is a strict subset of it, and three lint errors reached main.\n\nThat belongs to this item's fourth and second acceptance criteria rather than to a new one: local and hosted invocations of every quality gate must be proven equivalent, or the divergence declared per gate with a reason. Today there is no such proof and no such declaration, so the divergence is discoverable only by pushing.\n\nRecording both instances here so the remediation is scoped to the general property. The ambient-environment leak and the subset-command mismatch are two mechanisms for the same defect: a maintainer cannot learn from a local run what hosted CI will say."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-30T12:35:27.802Z"}],"before_hash":"299d03e119c0f814435fbd6960bce1d2aa4b943146c6ef581ce3b34f17603e3c","after_hash":"85c6a0910a4ae632d41d8227dc33bdfe34e5c912670716905de9e93aa95ce1f0","item_hash_version":3}
